    {
      "sectionId": "section-disclaimer",
      "heading": "Understanding RPGBOT’s Rating System",
      "sourceAnchor": "disclaimer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "RPGBOT uses a color coding scheme which is simple to understand and easy to read at a glance. This system is designed to help players make informed decisions for their dnd character builds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Red"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Bad, useless options, or options which\n\t\tare extremely situational. Nearly never useful."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Orange"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": OK options, or useful options\n\t\tthat only apply in rare circumstances. Useful sometimes."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Green"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Good options. Useful often."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Blue"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Fantastic options, often essential\n\t\tto the function of your character. Useful very frequently."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The advice offered below is based on the current "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "State of the 2014 DnD 5e Character Optimization Meta",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/state-of-the-meta/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " as of when the article was last updated. Keep in mind that the state of the meta periodically changes as new source materials are released, and the article will be updated accordingly as time allows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We will not include 3rd-party content, Unearthed Arcnaa content, or homebrew in guides for official content because we can’t assume that your game will allow them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-animal-enhancement",
      "heading": "Animal Enhancement",
      "sourceAnchor": "animal-enhancement",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-animal-enhancement-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "You get one choice of Animal Enhancement at 1st level and another at 5th.\n\tThere are only 3 choices at each level. At 5th level you can choose a new\n\toption from the 1st-level list, but there’s little reason to do so."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-animal-enhancement-1",
      "parentSectionId": "section-animal-enhancement",
      "heading": "Level 1",
      "sourceAnchor": "animal-enhancement-1",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-animal-enhancement-1-1",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Manta Glide"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Feather Fall is a 1st-level\n\t\tspell which makes this almost totally obsolete."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Nimble Climber"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Climb speeds aren’t as\n\t\tgood as fly speeds, but they’re the next-best thing and you can still\n\t\tcircumvent many obstacles by climbing."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Underwater Adaptation"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Unless you’re in\n\t\tan aquatic campaign, this won’t see much use. Usually you can get spells to\n\t\thandle occasional encounters with water."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-animal-enhancement-5",
      "parentSectionId": "section-animal-enhancement",
      "heading": "Level 5",
      "sourceAnchor": "animal-enhancement-5",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-animal-enhancement-5-1",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Acid Spit"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Single-target with mediocre\n\t\tdamage. It’s as much damage as a cantrip like Fire Bolt, and since it works\n\t\ton your Constitution modifier for the save DC it’s going to have a lower DC\n\t\tthan your attacks/spells until you can afford to increase your Constitution.\n\t\tHonestly the fact that this has limited uses is a pointless limitation. The\n\t\tability isn’t good enough that it needs a usage limitation."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Carapace"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": AC bonuses are always great, but\n\t\tit doesn’t apply if you’re wearing heavy armor so classes like the Fighter\n\t\tand the Paladin should look elsewhere. For other classes, this is the go-to\n\t\toption at this level."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Grappling Appendages"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": As much damage as a\n\t\tclub, and after hitting you can grapple as a Bonus Action. If you’re\n\t\tproficient in Athletics and have good Strength this can be a great combo. By\n\t\tthis level martial classes have Extra Attack, so you can Shove a foe prone,\n\t\thit them with a claw with Advantage since they’re prone, then Grapple them\n\t\tas a Bonus Action to prevent them from standing or crawling away."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Simic Hybrid Classes",
      "sourceAnchor": "classes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-classes-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Because the custom origin rules change things so little for the Simic Hybrid,\n\tthe custom origin rules are not addressed in a separate section as I have done\n\tin most of my race handbooks."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-artificer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Artificer",
      "sourceAnchor": "artificer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-artificer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Put the flexible ability score increase into Intelligence, and you’re good to\n\tgo. At 5th level pick up Carapace, and even in medium armor you can hit 20 AC\n\tbefore you look at all of your Infused Items."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-barbarian",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Barbarian",
      "sourceAnchor": "barbarian",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-barbarian-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Strength, Constitution, and Darkvision are a great start. Carapace at 5th\n\tlevel works great, and if you somehow manage 20 Dexterity and 20 Constitution\n\tyou can have an AC of 21 totally naked (23 with a shield!)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-barbarian-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Path of the Beast’s Beastial Soul (Jumping) allows you to easily jump very\n\thigh into the air, potentially spending your entire move speed on a high jump.\n\tIf you combine that with Manta Glide, you can get a bunch of extra movement\n\twithout dashing. For example: If you jump 30 feet into the air, you can then\n\tmove 60 feet horizontally by gliding and land without taking falling damage,\n\tallowing you to move long distances very quickly without needing to Dash."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-bard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Bard",
      "sourceAnchor": "bard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-bard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Constitution, Charisma, Darkvision. You don’t need much else, but Animal\n\tEnhancements may save you some spells."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-cleric",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Cleric",
      "sourceAnchor": "cleric",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-cleric-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Constitution, Wisdom, Darkvision. You don’t need much else, but Animal\n\tEnhancements may save you some spells."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-druid",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Druid",
      "sourceAnchor": "druid",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-druid-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Constitution, Wisdom, Darkvision. You don’t need much else, but Animal\n\tEnhancements may save you some spells. Wild Shape will notably cause you to\n\tlose most of your racial features, so avoid Circle of the Moon."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-fighter",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Fighter",
      "sourceAnchor": "fighter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fighter-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Grappling Appendages feels like it was made for the Fighter. If you miss,\n\tyou’ll have a bunch of additional attacks to try to set up the\n\tShove+Claw+Grapple combo, then once they’re on the ground you can use a\n\ttwo-handed weapon and deal big piles of damage."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-monk",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Monk",
      "sourceAnchor": "monk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-monk-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The climb speed and the swim speed from the 1st-level Animal Enhancements\n\tboth match your land speed, which means that the Monk’s ever-increasing land\n\tspeed also improves the additional movement type granted by your enhancement.\n\tAt 5th level you could take Grappling Appendages if you like to grapple, but\n\tit will conflict with Martial Arts. Most likely you’ll take Carapace instead,\n\twhich is a great choice on a class with low hit points which is locked into\n\tmelee combat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-monk-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If you use the custom origin rules, you can move the increases to Dexterity\n\tand Wisdom. Starting with 16 in each gives you an AC of 17, higher than any\n\tother monk can achieve at first level with the exception of the Tortle."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-paladin",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Paladin",
      "sourceAnchor": "paladin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-paladin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Paladin is probably the Simic Hybrid’s worst choice for a front-line\n\tmartial class, though that doesn’t mean that it’s a bad choice. Your options\n\tfor useful Animal Enhancements are really limited, and you won’t benefit from\n\tGrappling Appendages as much as the Fighter because paladins get fewer attacks\n\tto capitalize on the Shove+Claw+Grapple combo."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-ranger",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Ranger",
      "sourceAnchor": "ranger",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ranger-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "With Carapace you can match the AC of a heavily-armored character, and with\n\tthe Constitution increase you can offset the relatively poor hit die compared\n\tto front-line martial classes like the Fighter and the Paladin. A\n\tStrength-based build could absolutely work here, but a Dexterity-based build\n\twill likely still be easier and more effective."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-rogue",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Rogue",
      "sourceAnchor": "rogue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-rogue-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Climb speeds are great for rogues since most enemies are accustomed to other\n\tcreatures getting around on the ground. Tragically Grappling Appendages isn’t\n\tgreat for Sneak Attack, so you’re mostly locked into Carapace at 5th level.\n\tIt’s not a bad thing to be stuck with, but it would still be nice to have\n\tother viable options."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-sorcerer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Sorcerer",
      "sourceAnchor": "sorcerer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-sorcerer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Constitution, Charisma, Darkvision. You don’t need much else, but Animal\n\tEnhancements may save you some spells."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-warlock",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Warlock",
      "sourceAnchor": "warlock",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-warlock-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Constitution, Charisma, Darkvision. You don’t need much else, but Animal\n\tEnhancements may save you some spells."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-wizard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Wizard",
      "sourceAnchor": "wizard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-wizard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Constitution, Intelligence, Darkvision. You don’t need much else, but Animal\n\tEnhancements may save you some spells."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
